o she didn't share it. Therefore, she won't share \"Black Mirror\" to Lisa.\n\nWait, but the question is about \"Black Mirror.\" The context says she doesn't download it, but it doesn't say she doesn't watch it. Hmm, but the statement is about downloading, not watching. So, if she doesn't download it, she won't share it. \n\nBut wait, the context says that she only downloads shows she's binge-watched. So, if she didn't download it, she didn't watch it. Therefore, she didn't watch it, so she didn't share it. So, she won't share \"Black Mirror\" to Lisa.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the context doesn't specify whether she watches \"Stranger Things\" or not. It just says she will watch it because it's popular. So, she will watch \"Stranger Things,\" download it, and share it. But for \"Black Mirror,\" she doesn't download it, so she doesn't share it.\n\nSo, the statement is that she will share \"Black Mirror\" to Lisa. But since she doesn't download it, she won't share it. Therefore, the statement is false.\n\nWait, but let me make sure. The context says that if she doesn't download a show, she won't share it. So, since she doesn't download \"Black Mirror,\" she won't share it. Therefore, the statement is false.\n\nSo, the answer should be B) False.\n</think>\n\nThe statement is false because Karen does not download \"Black Mirror,\" so she won't share it with Lisa.\n\nAnswer: B) False",
