>\n\nThe statement is false. \n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**\n\n1. **Identify Taylor's Scenario:**\n   - From statement 7, Taylor is in one of two mutually exclusive scenarios:\n     a. She grew up in a health-conscious home AND has good parent relationships.\n     b. She did NOT grow up in a health-conscious home AND did NOT have good parent relationships.\n\n2. **Analyze Scenario a:**\n   - If Taylor grew up in a health-conscious home (statement 2), she would eat salads regularly.\n   - However, statement 5 states that if she has good parent relationships, she does NOT eat salads. This creates a contradiction, so scenario a is impossible.\n\n3. **Analyze Scenario b:**\n   - Taylor did NOT grow up in a health-conscious home, so statement 3 implies she did NOT fulfill her daily nutritional intake.\n   - Statement 6 indicates that not fulfilling daily intake means she doesn't visit the gym at least once a day.\n   - Since Taylor didn't grow up health-conscious and didn't fulfill her intake, she doesn't meet the criteria in statement 1 to eat salads regularly.\n\n4. **Conclusion:**\n   - Taylor does not eat salads regularly, making the statement false.\n\n**Answer: B) False**",
