r binging, but not necessarily a necessary condition. So, she might have other reasons to binge other shows that aren't popular. But in this case, since she doesn't download \"Black Mirror,\" she doesn't binge it. \n\nSo, using the contrapositive, if she doesn't binge it, then it's not popular. Therefore, \"Black Mirror\" is not popular. \n\nSo, the statement \"Black Mirror\" is popular would be false. Therefore, the answer is B) False.\n</think>\n\nThe statement \"Black Mirror\" is popular is false. \n\nStep-by-step explanation:\n1. \"Stranger Things\" is popular, so Karen binges it.\n2. Karen only downloads shows she binges, so she downloads \"Stranger Things.\"\n3. \"Black Mirror\" is a Netflix show, but Karen doesn't download it, so she doesn't binge it.\n4. Since Karen doesn't binge \"Black Mirror,\" it's not a popular show (contrapositive of the first statement).\n\nAnswer: B) False",
