ns or funny, he ends up being yellow. Therefore, \"ugly or yellow\" is true because he's yellow.\n\nWait, but let me check again. If Ben is from The Simpsons, he's yellow. If Ben is funny, he's from The Simpsons, so he's yellow. So in either case, he's yellow. Therefore, \"ugly or yellow\" is true because he's yellow. So the statement is true.\n\nWait, but earlier I thought that if he's from The Simpsons, he's yellow, so he's yellow, making the statement true. If he's funny, he's from The Simpsons, so he's yellow. So in both cases, he's yellow, so \"ugly or yellow\" is true because he's yellow. Therefore, the statement is true.\n\nSo the answer should be A) True.\n</think>\n\nThe statement \"Ben is ugly or yellow\" is true because in both scenarios (whether Ben is from The Simpsons or funny), he ends up being yellow. Therefore, the statement is true.\n\nA) True\n\nAnswer: A",
