ibility? Let me think.\n\nThe statement says, \"If Rock is neither a fly nor a bird, then Rock neither flies nor breathes.\" So, Rock isn't a fly, and Rock isn't a bird. From the context, since all animals are either monkeys or birds, Rock isn't an animal. So, Rock isn't a monkey or a bird, which are animals. Therefore, Rock isn't an animal, so it doesn't breathe because all animals breathe. Wait, but the statement says that if Rock isn't a fly or a bird, then it neither flies nor breathes. So, Rock doesn't fly (given) and doesn't breathe (because it's not an animal). \n\nBut the question is about whether Rock has wings. From the context, all birds fly and have wings. Since Rock isn't a bird, it doesn't have wings. So, Rock doesn't fly, and since it's not a bird, it doesn't have wings either. \n\nWait, but the statement says that if Rock isn't a fly or a bird, then it neither flies nor breathes. So, Rock doesn't fly, and it doesn't breathe. But the question is about wings. Since Rock isn't a bird, it doesn't have wings. So, Rock doesn't have wings. \n\nBut let me make sure I'm not missing anything. The context says all animals are either monkeys or birds, so Rock isn't an animal. Therefore, Rock isn't a monkey or a bird. Since all birds fly, Rock isn't a bird, so it doesn't fly. The statement also says that if Rock isn't a fly or a bird, then it neither flies nor breathes. So, Rock doesn't fly, and it doesn't breathe. \n\nBut the question is about wings. Since Rock isn't a bird, it doesn't have wings. So, Rock doesn't have wings. Therefore, the statement \"Rock has wings\" would be false. \n\nWait, but the last part says that if Rock isn't a fly or a bird, then it neither flies nor breathes. So, Rock doesn't fly, and it doesn't breathe. But the question is about wings, which are related to flying. Since Rock isn't a bird, it doesn't have wings. So, Rock doesn't have wings. \n\nSo, the answer should be that Rock does not have wings, making the statement \"Rock has wings\" false. Therefore, the answer is B) False.\n</think>\n\nThe statement \"Rock has wings\" is false because Rock is neither a bird nor a fly, and since all birds have wings, Rock cannot have wings.\n\nAnswer: B) False",
